In article <1qhid6$mlm@pith.uoregon.edu> seth@cie-2.uoregon.edu (Master Nethacker) writes:
>Albert Wammes (wammes@sun034.research.ptt.nl) wrote:
>: Hi Hackers,

>: a couple of times I got the following message when wishing for an item
>: (i.e. Mjollnir and yendorian express card):

>: "you feel an item in your hand and then it disappears"

>: What does this message mean, and how come??

>Albert, I couldn't tell you why it disappears, but I _can_ tell you for sure
>that some items just can't be used by just anyone.  F.ex., _only_ a lawful
>Samurai can wield the Tsurugi of Muramasa-- anyone else will get blasted,
>and the weapon slips out of grasp.  In general, I'd say don't bother wishing
>for quest items-- if you aren't the right class, you (probably!  not sure..)
>can't use it, and if you _can_ use it, you might experience problems in your
>quest, at least at this patchlevel.

If you are the right class *or* the right alignment when you pick up the 
item you can use it (even if the alignment is from the helm of opposite 
alignment).

However you have a 2/(number of artifacts in the game) chance of getting an 
artifact when wishing for it, so wish for artifacts before sacrificing for 
them (or questing for them).  You should not wish for your quest item.
